Shadows flicker over the walls of a chamber of Hell, complemented by the
screams of tortured lemures.  The two-headed Overlord waits and watches.

Tip, tip, tap, tap ... footsteps float up the staircase.  Elven footsteps.
Asmodeus grins.  A fresh soul approaches!

Tip, tip, tap, tap ... what's this?  An unshriven soul!  An Elf who has
not passed through the gates of death, who has not been ferried by
Charon, who still bears hope!  Not to mention a bespoke bow and a
quiver of soul searing blessed arrows.

And how did this never-killed Elf manage to approach from the LOWER
staircase?

Well, one doesn't get to be the Overlord of Hell by being timid.
On the other hand, one cannot strike first at a still-living soul.

Asmodeus draws himself up to his full 20 foot height.  One head
snarls, and one head screams.

  "INSOLENT ELF!  HOW DARE YOU --"
    "-- TRAVERSE THE REALM OF ASMODEUS --"
      "-- WITHOUT MY LEAVE!"
  "THE PRICE OF A SAFE CONDUCT --"
    "-- IS 125 ZORKMIDS --"
      "-- OR YOUR LIFE AND SOUL!"

Ellora pauses and looks the Overlord up and down.  She pulls a
well-thumbed one-volume encyclopedia out of her backpack and starts
leafing through the A's.

  "Hang on, I think this book says something about you ..."
  "CONSULT NOT THY BOOK!"

Ellora squints at Asmodeus.

  "Hmmm, how peaceful are you, really?"
  "I AM LOSING PATIENCE, ELF!"

Ellora looks around the chamber, obviously stalling for time.

  "Hey!  What's that wand over there in the corner?"
  "NO!  NO LOOKING!  I SAID, 125 ZORKMIDS!"

Ellora stands quietly for a moment, thinking.  On the one hand,
125 zorkmids is a lot of money.  That's enough to buy 2 or 3
food rations, or a minor consultation or two from the Oracle.

On the other hand, there's a 20 foot tall two-headed demon overlord
sharing the room with her.  And he wants an answer, NOW.

Ellora can't recall what her mini-encyclopedia said about Asmodeus,
but she makes an intuitive guess that he's not real big on patience.

  "Oh, all right.  Here's 125 zorkmids.  And a tip.  Keep the change."

